counterexample:
-- No counterexample exists under standard SQL semantics, as the queries are logically equivalent.
-- Any dataset will yield the same result for both queries.
-- For example, if table1 contains:
-- INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (10), (20), (30), (30), (40);
-- Q1 would return 40 (unique values are 10, 20, 40; max is 40).
-- Q2 would return 40 (unique values are 10, 20, 40; ORDER BY DESC LIMIT 1 yields 40; MAX(40) is 40).
-- If table1 contains:
-- INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (10), (10), (20), (20);
-- Both Q1 and Q2 would return NULL (no value appears exactly once).
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (10), (20), (30), (30), (40);

